# Glissa Sunslayer's third mode on a creature, with "up to three" taking fewer: Bot2's Ornithopter has a flying, a first
# strike and a lifelink counter (from its Abigale); Bot1 removes two of the three kinds and the first strike counter stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Glissa Sunslayer
Forest x3
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Black Lotus
Abigale, Eloquent First-Year
Ornithopter
Plains x3
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Glissa Sunslayer.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot2.Hand.Abigale, Eloquent First-Year.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Flying = 1
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Glissa Sunslayer)
Bot1.Modes(Remove up to three counters)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.RemoveCounters(Ornithopter: Flying 1; Ornithopter: Lifelink 1)

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Flying = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Lifelink = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.FirstStrike = 1
